  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class C4 (HMO-house in multiple occupation) (RETROSPECTIVE).",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be retained in accordance with the following approved plans:\rFIRE SAFETY / MEANS OF ESCAPE NOTE\rSection Elevation Plan\rBins\rCycle storage\rFirst floor plan\rGround floor plan\rRoof plan\rLocation Plan & Block Plan\rLocation Plan & Block Plan\rLevel 3 Flood Risk Assessment\rFLOOD EVACUATION PLAN\rPLANNING STATEMENT\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 5 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The refuse storage facilities shown on drawing titled \"BINS\" shall be provided and retained in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The cycle storage facilities shown on drawing titled \"EXISTING CYCLE STORAGE\" shall be provided and retained in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the kitchen/dining room shall be retained as such, in accordance with the approved plans, in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r"
  ],
